{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor consistently prioritized the right breast BI-RADS 4B lesion for tissue diagnosis while avoiding premature cancer certainty, used workspace/record review and targeted questioning, and repeatedly converted fragmented information into actionable follow-up. The trajectory also maintained perioperative and postoperative safety boundaries, red flags, pathology uncertainty, and medication limits. Multiple high-order points were actively completed, including repairing confusion between observation and excision, document/navigation support, dynamic reprioritization after pathology and referral updates, and safe bounded closure with family receipt. No responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect is evident, so the deterministic boundary supports grade 5.",
